# Davart mobile UI

## Default skill stack (pick one primary)

| Job | Skill |
|-----|--------|
| Build / extend product screens | `interface-design` |
| iOS feel, nav, touch targets | `ios-hig-design` |
| Fix hierarchy, spacing, type | `ui-refactor` |
| UX review (no code yet) | `ux-heuristics` |

Optional polish only if the screen still looks generic: `impeccable` or `redesign-existing-projects`.

Do **not** stack hallmark / taste / frontend-design-pro for in-app Flutter work — those target marketing/web aesthetics.

## Hard constraints

- Reuse `apps/mobile/lib/core/widgets/ds/` — do not invent parallel buttons/cards/inputs.
- Colors only via `AppColors.of(context)` (`lib/core/theme/app_colors.dart`) — `DavartColors` ThemeExtension for light/dark. Accent is yellow `#FFDD2D`. Static `AppColors.*` fields are the light palette (splash / const only).
- Theme via `AppTheme` — no one-off hex in feature screens unless extending tokens.
- Keep 5-tab shell: Магазин · Дизайн · Чаты · Корзина · Профиль. Bottom nav always visible on tab roots; product/checkout push above the shell.
- Prefer calm retail UI: neutral surfaces (white in light, near-black in dark), yellow accent CTAs, strong type hierarchy — not purple gradients, glow, or dense dashboard chrome.
- Load `.interface-design/system.md` when using `interface-design`; offer to update it after new patterns.

## Prompt shape for the user

`use interface-design — <screen> — keep DS widgets and AppColors`
